yst_adjustment": 2.23, "key_factors": ["Election-night results and multiple outlets confirm Dembo defeated Alvarado and flipped the seat", "Late October polls showed Dembo consistently ahead by 6-9 points", "Dembo out-raised Alvarado and drew more outside support", "Open seat after Barr's retirement removed the incumbent advantage"], "rationale": "The race has been decided: outlets across the spectrum report Alvarado conceded and Dembo won, returning KY-6 to Democratic hands despite its Trump +15 lean. Late polling and Dembo's fundraising edge pointed the same direction.", "watch": "Nothing remains to watch; only final certified vote totals could adjust the exact margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Andy Barr (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kentucky's 6th District was rated a tossup through Election Day, with most analysts split between Tossup and Lean R after Andy Barr retired to run for Senate. Democrat Zach Dembo out-raised Republican Ralph Alvarado and led in the final round of surveys, though nearly all came from Democratic-leaning sponsors. The district's Republican lean of about seven points made an upset plausible, and prediction markets briefly priced the race as decided.\n\nThe outcome resolved decisively for Democrats: on November 4, outlets including the Courier-Journal, The Hill, and local Kentucky broadcasters reported Dembo's victory and Alvarado's concession, flipping a seat Trump carried by double digits. The result stands as a Democratic hold going forward.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2515, "margin": -3.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.296, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2877, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2982, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2389, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2735, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2956, "margin": -4.0}, {"d